### What is the redrive flow?

Redrive is the controlled process of moving records from the dead letter queue back to the main processing flow so that the now-fixed consumer can handle them. It begins only after the root-cause bug is fixed and deployed.

```java
package com.bank.redrive;

public class RedrivePrerequisites {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Redrive prerequisites:");
        System.out.println("  1. Root cause identified");
        System.out.println("  2. Fix deployed and verified");
        System.out.println("  3. DLT records inspected and classified");
        System.out.println("  4. Replay tool configured with throttling");
        System.out.println("  5. Consumers confirmed idempotent");
    }
}
```

```text
Redrive prerequisites:
  1. Root cause identified
  2. Fix deployed and verified
  3. DLT records inspected and classified
  4. Replay tool configured with throttling
  5. Consumers confirmed idempotent
```

### How do you inspect DLT records?

Read the DLT records and their error headers to classify each one: transient failure now resolved, permanent failure to discard, or record needing manual correction.

```java
package com.bank.redrive;

import org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.ConsumerRecord;
import org.apache.kafka.common.header.Header;
import java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets;

public class DltInspector {
    public static void inspect(ConsumerRecord<String, String> record) {
        System.out.println("DLT Record:");
        System.out.println("  Key    : " + record.key());
        System.out.println("  Value  : " + record.value());
        for (Header header : record.headers()) {
            String value = new String(header.value(), StandardCharsets.UTF_8);
            System.out.println("  Header : " + header.key() + " = " + value);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Classification:");
        System.out.println("  REPLAY  : DatabaseTimeout -> fix deployed, will succeed");
        System.out.println("  DISCARD : MalformedJSON   -> garbage, cannot replay");
        System.out.println("  MANUAL  : InvalidAmount   -> needs data correction");
    }
}
```

```text
Classification:
  REPLAY  : DatabaseTimeout -> fix deployed, will succeed
  DISCARD : MalformedJSON   -> garbage, cannot replay
  MANUAL  : InvalidAmount   -> needs data correction
```

### How do you selectively replay records?

Republish records to a dedicated reprocessing topic rather than the live main topic. Preserve the original key so partitioning and ordering semantics are respected. Throttle the replay rate.

```java
package com.bank.redrive;

import org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.ConsumerRecord;
import org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.ConsumerRecords;
import org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.KafkaConsumer;
import org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.KafkaProducer;
import org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.ProducerRecord;
import java.time.Duration;

public class RedriveReplayTool {
    public static void replay(KafkaConsumer<String, String> dltConsumer,
                               KafkaProducer<String, String> producer,
                               String reprocessTopic,
                               int throttleMs) throws InterruptedException {
        ConsumerRecords<String, String> records = dltConsumer.poll(Duration.ofSeconds(5));
        int replayed = 0;
        int discarded = 0;

        for (ConsumerRecord<String, String> record : records) {
            if (shouldReplay(record)) {
                // Preserve original key for correct partitioning
                producer.send(new ProducerRecord<>(
                    reprocessTopic, record.key(), record.value()));
                replayed++;
                Thread.sleep(throttleMs);  // Throttle
            } else {
                discarded++;
            }
        }
        dltConsumer.commitSync();
        System.out.println("Replayed: " + replayed + ", Discarded: " + discarded);
    }

    private static boolean shouldReplay(ConsumerRecord<String, String> record) {
        // Check error headers to classify
        return record.value() != null && !record.value().isEmpty();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Replay to reprocessing topic (not main):");
        System.out.println("  Isolates replay traffic from live traffic");
        System.out.println("  Allows independent throttling");
        System.out.println("  Preserves original key for partition mapping");
    }
}
```

```text
Replay to reprocessing topic (not main):
  Isolates replay traffic from live traffic
  Allows independent throttling
  Preserves original key for partition mapping
```

### Why must consumers be idempotent?

A record may have partially processed before failing. On replay, the consumer might see it again. Without idempotency, that means double debits or double fees.

```java
package com.bank.consumer;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

public class IdempotentSettlement {
    // Track processed transfer IDs
    private static final ConcurrentHashMap<String, Boolean> processedIds =
        new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public static void settle(String transferId, String accountId,
                               BigDecimal amount) {
        if (processedIds.putIfAbsent(transferId, true) != null) {
            System.out.println("  " + transferId + ": already settled, SKIP");
            return;
        }
        System.out.println("  " + transferId + ": settling " +
            amount + " INR for " + accountId);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        BigDecimal amount = new BigDecimal("50000.00");
        settle("TXN-001", "SAV2001", amount);  // First time
        settle("TXN-001", "SAV2001", amount);  // Replay -- skipped
        settle("TXN-002", "SAV3045", amount);  // New transfer
    }
}
```

```text
  TXN-001: settling 50000.00 INR for SAV2001
  TXN-001: already settled, SKIP
  TXN-002: settling 50000.00 INR for SAV3045
```

### What is the re-poisoning anti-pattern?

Blindly looping the entire DLT back to the main topic causes still-poisonous records to fail again and re-fill the DLT or stall the pipeline.

```java
package com.bank.mistake;

public class RePoisoningAntiPattern {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // WRONG: blind loop
        System.out.println("WRONG: pipe ALL DLT records back to main topic");
        System.out.println("  Permanent failures fail again -> back to DLT");
        System.out.println("  Infinite loop if auto-redrive is enabled");
        System.out.println();

        // CORRECT: inspect, classify, selectively replay
        System.out.println("CORRECT: inspect, classify, selective replay");
        System.out.println("  Transient -> replay to reprocessing topic");
        System.out.println("  Permanent -> discard with audit trail");
        System.out.println("  Unknown   -> manual investigation");
    }
}
```

```text
WRONG: pipe ALL DLT records back to main topic
  Permanent failures fail again -> back to DLT
  Infinite loop if auto-redrive is enabled

CORRECT: inspect, classify, selective replay
  Transient -> replay to reprocessing topic
  Permanent -> discard with audit trail
  Unknown   -> manual investigation
```

