### What are common mistakes during redrive?

The most dangerous mistake is replaying DLT records without first confirming the bug fix is deployed, which sends them right back to the DLT. Another error is replaying the entire DLT at once without throttling, which can overwhelm the consumer group. A third mistake is not making consumers idempotent, so a record that was partially processed before failing gets duplicated on redrive.

```java
package com.bank.kafka;

public class RedriveMistakes {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("WRONG: replay without deploying the fix");
        System.out.println("  Records go back to DLT immediately (re-poisoning)");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("WRONG: replay entire DLT at once");
        System.out.println("  10,000 records flood the consumer group");
        System.out.println("  Downstream services overwhelmed");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("WRONG: consumer not idempotent");
        System.out.println("  Record partially processed before first failure");
        System.out.println("  Redrive creates duplicate side effects");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("CORRECT: deploy fix, replay in small batches, idempotent consumers");
    }
}
```

```text
Expected output:
WRONG: replay without deploying the fix
  Records go back to DLT immediately (re-poisoning)

WRONG: replay entire DLT at once
  10,000 records flood the consumer group
  Downstream services overwhelmed

WRONG: consumer not idempotent
  Record partially processed before first failure
  Redrive creates duplicate side effects

CORRECT: deploy fix, replay in small batches, idempotent consumers
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

Redrive is a deliberate, audited, rate-limited operator action, not an automatic loop. Track how many records were replayed, succeeded, and re-failed. A reprocessing topic plus idempotent consumers plus a dashboard makes redrive observable and reversible. The dead letter records must carry enough metadata to make targeted replay possible.
